{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01R1:title", "parent_tag": "01R1", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "risk_level": "R1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Conormal sheaf of an immersion", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-conormal-sheaf}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:a03cb20cd5a6e5bf84b74af352f0eb0182e33b6b8b602b4d518c37495dbf7804", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:82f29cb46d47ecccdebd6e0a98d4fe47927a1e700eeee16d7861b2cc3db23ec1", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01R1:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "01R1", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a closed immersion. Let\n<MATH_0002> be the corresponding quasi-coherent\nsheaf of ideals. Consider the short exact sequence\n<MATH_0003>\nof quasi-coherent sheaves on <MATH_0004>. Since the sheaf <MATH_0005>\nis annihilated by <MATH_0006> it corresponds to a sheaf on <MATH_0007> by\nLemma <REF_0001>. This quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0008>-module is called the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>conormal sheaf of <MATH_0009> in <MATH_0010><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nand is often simply denoted\n<MATH_0011> by the abuse of notation mentioned in\nSection <REF_0002>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nIn case <MATH_0012> is a (locally closed) immersion we define the\nconormal sheaf of <MATH_0013> as the conormal sheaf of the closed\nimmersion <MATH_0014>, where\n<MATH_0015>. It is often denoted\n<MATH_0016> where <MATH_0017> is the ideal sheaf\nof the closed immersion <MATH_0018>.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$i : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n0 \\to \\mathcal{I}^2 \\to \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{I}/\\mathcal{I}^2 \\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{I}/\\mathcal{I}^2$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0007": "$Z$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-i-star-equivalence}", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_Z$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "MATH_0009": "$Z$", "MATH_0010": "$X$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{I}/\\mathcal{I}^2$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{section-closed-immersions-quasi-coherent}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "MATH_0012": "$i : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$i$", "MATH_0014": "$i : Z \\to X \\setminus \\partial Z$", "MATH_0015": "$\\partial Z = \\overline{Z} \\setminus Z$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{I}/\\mathcal{I}^2$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0018": "$i : Z \\to X \\setminus \\partial Z$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:9ccfe4dbc4d177e90a2d7a37b7a2639b3583cef34bf943e15e4d80015b162c38", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d2e771e6152765a5504fc6f2aa8c1e7180dda2792dba918e6f69ff3483e4a009", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4efab0ed46d3cfcd737aea21575b936a9e4b73a8328a9f8988f9001a1c7e1ec4"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01R2:statement", "parent_tag": "01R1", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an immersion. The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>conormal sheaf\n<MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003> in <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> or the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>conormal sheaf of <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nis the quasi-coherent <MATH_0006>-module <MATH_0007>\ndescribed above.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i : Z \\to X$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_{Z/X}$", "MATH_0003": "$Z$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "MATH_0005": "$i$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_Z$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}/\\mathcal{I}^2$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-conormal-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:c627a16defeaf64b8f9f2764be7f5e313fb3e8b11ce677f389c734fa6deae5b8", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8b16348b25075cf84b871e35bc5ea30ad3306f8f189d28edda6457d2496a378b", "source_math_hash": "sha256:aa567a1e5fe536286a4807fad90b734a44720a0973b9b5d38cc4b0aa6635ad29"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01R1:prose-0002", "parent_tag": "01R1", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn <REF_0001> this sheaf is denoted\n<MATH_0001>. We will not follow this convention since we would\nlike to reserve the notation <MATH_0002>\nfor the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>normal sheaf of the immersion<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>. It is defined as\n<MATH_0003>\nprovided the conormal sheaf is of finite presentation (otherwise the\nnormal sheaf may not even be quasi-coherent). We will come back to the\nnormal sheaf later (insert future reference here).\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "REF_0001": "\\cite[IV Definition 16.1.2]{EGA}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{N}_{Z/X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{N}_{Z/X}$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\mathcal{N}_{Z/X} =\n\\SheafHom_{\\mathcal{O}_Z}(\\mathcal{C}_{Z/X}, \\mathcal{O}_Z) =\n\\SheafHom_{\\mathcal{O}_Z}(\\mathcal{I}/\\mathcal{I}^2, \\mathcal{O}_Z)\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:ee1cf10b71dd09b79a9a6d9a66c070117c6d089bdc6f0297b1dcd6041dc2fd60", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:72ee8a84bcb2bcf28cc9aa6a77df84f945311917539b608a95c4fd14f09f0f5a", "source_math_hash": "sha256:abcfb0f8c7c02e1997352dfbccd2286daa40e4d7d0b65b71982ccba2a92ebecf"}
